{"name":"The Fifth Sun","hex":"#f0e22c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fifth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["The ordinal form of the number five."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The person or thing in the fifth position.\n The fifth gear of a transmission.","The fifth gear of a transmission."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fifth"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Fifth Sun (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"The Fifth Sun is an Iranian Drama, Sci-Fi series. The series is directed by Alireza Afkhami. The series has also been aired on iFilm since November 2021."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fifth_Sun_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q5870871"},{"title":"Five Suns","blocks":[{"text":"In creation myths, the term \"Five Suns\" refers to the belief of certain Nahua cultures and Aztec peoples that the world has gone through five distinct cycles of creation and destruction, with the current era being the fifth. It is primarily derived from a combination of myths, cosmologies, and eschatological beliefs that were originally held by pre-Columbian peoples in the Mesoamerican region, including central Mexico, and it is part of a larger mythology of Fifth World or Fifth Sun beliefs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/File-Monolito_de_la_Piedra_del_Sol_%28centro%29.jpg/330px-File-Monolito_de_la_Piedra_del_Sol_%28centro%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Suns","wikidata":"Q786836"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun","wikidata":"Q525"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Pyramid_of_the_Moon_from_Pyramid_of_the_Sun%2C_Teotihuacan%2C_in_sunlight.jpg/500px-Pyramid_of_the_Moon_from_Pyramid_of_the_Sun%2C_Teotihuacan%2C_in_sunlight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Pyramid_of_the_Moon_from_Pyramid_of_the_Sun%2C_Teotihuacan%2C_in_sunlight.jpg/1280px-Pyramid_of_the_Moon_from_Pyramid_of_the_Sun%2C_Teotihuacan%2C_in_sunlight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Pyramid_of_the_Moon_from_Pyramid_of_the_Sun%2C_Teotihuacan%2C_in_sunlight.jpg/500px-Pyramid_of_the_Moon_from_Pyramid_of_the_Sun%2C_Teotihuacan%2C_in_sunlight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Teotihuacan, the \"birthplace of the gods\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APyramid_of_the_Moon_from_Pyramid_of_the_Sun%2C_Teotihuacan%2C_in_sunlight.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Codex_Borgia_page_71.jpg/500px-Codex_Borgia_page_71.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Codex_Borgia_page_71.jpg/1280px-Codex_Borgia_page_71.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_